# Review of #4471

The desk merged reports with similar subjects, but matching subjects do not establish a common cause. The export groups unique report IDs using the tenant's locale, booking form, and intake channel rather than the browser's intake tag.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Separate problems

- [Shared parser reads day-first tenant dates month-first](https://github.com/ppierzchalka/mega-s01e03-support-kb/issues/1). The parser group includes five reports the desk read as one-day shifts; investigate those separately before assuming the parser caused them.
- [Booking-v3 shows a month-first hint for day-first tenants](https://github.com/ppierzchalka/mega-s01e03-support-kb/issues/2). On the form, users follow the hint but the date is interpreted in the tenant's order.

The classification is not proof of the root cause of every individual report. Confirm the one-day-shift cases and reassess the counts if the evidence supports another cause. Merge reports by demonstrated cause, not subject alone; do not edit the accepted decision record in place.

## The queue

The desk received reports for months before the bulk merge. A merged count is not the same thing as the date reports arrived, and the desk continues to work after the export. Refresh the source data before relying on these totals.

